{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Prerequisite: Dragonborn\n\nNote: This Feat is intended to use instead of the regular Dragon Fear feat.\n\nYou have awakened the inner natural power of dragons to inspire fear and, when angered, you radiate menace. You gain the following benefits:\n\n- Increase your Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n\n- Frightful Presence: At the start of your turn, you can force each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you to make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier). A target automatically succeeds on the save if it can\u0027t hear or see you. On a failed save, a target becomes frightened for 1 minute. If the frightened target takes any damage, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature\u0027s saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to this feature for the next 24 hours.","level":1}],"id":"dragon_fear","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Dragon Fear [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}